  "description": "This skill should be used when the user has an approved Design Plan and wants to build their AI workflow. It sets up the workflow's place with the user, builds each task in the plan (skills, agents, connections and any schedule), checks each one against what it must do without making any real change, then saves or installs the workflow where it runs and writes a build record that says what was built and what it can access. Also use when the user says \"continue my workflow\" and the workflow needs building: an approved plan not built yet, a build that stopped partway, misses from a test round for Build to fix, or an approved change to a workflow that's already live. Not for \"build my knowledge graph\": that is the building-knowledge-graph skill. This is the Build step of the AI Workflow Framework.",
